  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1249 PM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nFrom Wednesday through Friday, Iowa will continue to reside \nbeneath northwesterly 500 MB steering flow, though which at \nleast two more shortwave impulses will travel overhead. At the \nsurface, however, the old decayed frontal zone should be pushed \nto our south over Missouri by convective outflows from \nTuesday/Tuesday night storms. Additional showers may linger in \nour southern counties Wednesday into Wednesday night, but then \ndecrease from Thursday onward with generally 10-30% POPs in the \nextended. The quick passage of a surface ridge along with light \nnorthwesterly flow should also allow for somewhat cooler \nweather, with daily highs generally in the 70s to lower 80s, \nthough dewpoints will likely remain in the 60s to lower 70s. \nThere are some indications that next weekend a larger surface \nhigh pressure system will build into the Upper Midwest and \nGreat Lakes region, which if this occurs, may provide more \ntangible relief from the humidity that has persisted for the \npast few weeks.",
